            "review_title": "Review at Le Gia Seafood",
            "review_text": "Nhuy T\nMelbourne, Australia3 contributions\n0\nBad service and overpriced for mediocre meals\nJan 2016 • Family\nThis was the only let down in our entire trip in da nang. The service was terrible we ordered three dishes; squid with tomatoes and pineapple, seafood fried noodles and garlic water spinach. The first two took about half an hour to arrive at which point I was still able to over looked due to the it being busy. But the quality of the food was an instant let down the squid was over cooked and basically rubber. The garlic water spinach which should have taken no more that 3 minutes to make came over an hour later after we had finished all the mains, and yes we did asked about it five times. It wasn't until we gave up and decided to leave that the spinach was brought to us, to my disbelief they insisted that we still had to pay for it. I wasn't in the mood to argue so we took care of the bill and will never return\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 27, 2016",
