            "review_title": "Review at Le Gia Seafood",
            "review_text": "trailfinder58\nKent, England57 contributions\n0\nGreat seafood restaurant\nFeb 2014 • Couples\nWe found this great seafood restaurant off the beaten track near one of the bridges in Da Nang. It quickly became a favourite and we ate there 3 times. It has great live seafood at very good prices. Da Nang has many top quality seafood restaurants - mainly near the beach (and if they are on the beach then the prices are much higher!) so the standard is set high. Although there are restaurants with a bigger range of seafood - this small place still had about a dozen tanks with fresh seafood ranging from small muscles to large crabs. The cooking styles were simple and not fancy but that was fine as it was the taste of fresh seafood we wanted. Our average price for a very filling meal with drinks for 2 was £14. Just a note to say we only ate there one evening as we saw 5 or 6 rats running around the floors (it is an open restaurant so no doors or windows there to keep them out) so if youre nervous about them its better to go for lunch!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 20, 2014",
